      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BING BING SLAYER (5) was prominent early from the tricky draw and did a fair job to be beaten 4.5 lengths into second (31.10) at this track in a Grade 6 over 531m. Rates highly and will give a great sight. KILCOY GEM (2) hit the ground running last time with a hot early split and tried to lead throughout but had to settle for the minors when second (31.03) at this track over 531m. Goes very well from this draw with two wins and two minor placings from five starts. Leading chance. DOLAN (4) jumped from box 1 last time and ran away with an impressive win scoring by 4.5 lengths at this track in a handy 30.78. Has the squeeze box to overcome and will need the breaks early. In sparkling form with a string of wins and can measure up again. YOU SEE ME (1) missed the placings here most recently but can sneak into the finish with the right run.",
